<!-- Add this section to create_table.sgml after the USING method parameter description -->

   <para>
    <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> includes multiple table access methods:
   </para>

   <itemizedlist>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      <literal>heap</literal> - The default row-oriented storage with
      multi-version concurrency control. Best for general-purpose OLTP and
      mixed workloads.
     </para>
    </listitem>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      <literal>recno</literal> - Time-based MVCC storage with in-place updates,
      integrated overflow pages, and built-in compression. Optimized for
      update-heavy OLTP workloads. See <xref linkend="recno"/> for details.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </itemizedlist>

   <para>
    Example using RECNO storage for an update-heavy table:
   </para>

<programlisting>
CREATE TABLE user_sessions (
    session_id uuid PRIMARY KEY,
    user_id bigint NOT NULL,
    last_activity timestamptz NOT NULL,
    session_data jsonb,
    ip_address inet
) USING recno;
</programlisting>

   <para>
    RECNO is particularly effective for tables that:
   </para>

   <itemizedlist>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Experience frequent <command>UPDATE</command> operations
     </para>
    </listitem>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Have large text or JSON columns that would benefit from integrated
      overflow storage instead of TOAST
     </para>
    </listitem>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Would benefit from automatic attribute-level compression
     </para>
    </listitem>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Need to avoid transaction ID wraparound issues
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </itemizedlist>

   <para>
    Storage parameters specific to RECNO can be set with the <literal>WITH</literal>
    clause:
   </para>

<programlisting>
CREATE TABLE events (
    id bigserial PRIMARY KEY,
    event_time timestamptz NOT NULL,
    event_type text NOT NULL,
    payload jsonb
) USING recno
WITH (
    recno_compression_level = 6,
    recno_overflow_threshold = 2048
);
</programlisting>